/*
 * Declares the RangeType class.
 *
 * A RangeType represents a numeric range defined by a starting integer and a
 * step value. Ranges are used to describe iteration domains and arithmetic
 * progressions. Both the start and step types are integers, and their
 * mutability is derived from the mutability of the range itself.
 *
 * Ranges:
 *   - wrap two integer types: the start value type and the step type,
 *   - cannot contain movable types,
 *   - do not borrow data,
 *   - have simple mutability semantics: only the outer mutability matters.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native::compound::range
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native/compound/range.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
